{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JJeWkwxpjLZSG6arWnMSwr","type":"tool_result","content":"chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:561:🗺️ **Chapter 3 · Voyage Progress:** census complete → now the arrangement → then the loop\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-562-\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-563----\n--\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:746:🌊 **Chapter 3 · Voyage Progress:** census complete → arrangement complete → now the loop\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-747-\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-748----\n--\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:904:🌅 **Chapter 3 · Voyage Progress:** census → arrangement → **loop complete**\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-905-\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-906----\n--\nchapter-04-records-of-intent.md:1176:**Voyage Progress:** 🗺️ → 🌊 → 🌅 — Chapter 4 of 15 complete. You have crossed from *watching the system* to *writing to it*, which is the largest single step in this book.\nchapter-04-records-of-intent.md-1177-\nchapter-04-records-of-intent.md-1178-You can now read a manifest you have never seen. You know which of its fields you author and which one is a report. You know where its name has to be unique and which resources have no name-scope at all. You know how to describe a set of objects rather than list one. And you know the exact thing a Secret does and does not do, which is a piece of knowledge a surprising number of working practitioners have wrong.\n=== DIFFICULTY LEGEND CH1 ===\n162:## ⚪ What the KCNA Is, and Who It's For\n186:## ⚪ Ninety Minutes: The Exam as Published\n366:## ⚪ The Phrase We Haven't Defined Yet\n388:## ⚪ How This Book Is Built\n437:Difficulty is marked on section headings: ⚪ Foundation, 🔵 Standard, 🟡 Advanced, 🔴 Expert.\n457:## ⚪ Three Ways to Read This Book","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"336032f7-3fe6-40fe-8d51-cccd5fc8c432","uuid":"b32c1d3b-acc2-4459-a74f-8be8c34ea8d5","timestamp":"2026-08-24T11:16:56.500Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:561:🗺️ **Chapter 3 · Voyage Progress:** census complete → now the arrangement → then the loop\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-562-\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-563----\n--\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:746:🌊 **Chapter 3 · Voyage Progress:** census complete → arrangement complete → now the loop\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-747-\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-748----\n--\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:904:🌅 **Chapter 3 · Voyage Progress:** census → arrangement → **loop complete**\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-905-\nchapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-906----\n--\nchapter-04-records-of-intent.md:1176:**Voyage Progress:** 🗺️ → 🌊 → 🌅 — Chapter 4 of 15 complete. You have crossed from *watching the system* to *writing to it*, which is the largest single step in this book.\nchapter-04-records-of-intent.md-1177-\nchapter-04-records-of-intent.md-1178-You can now read a manifest you have never seen. You know which of its fields you author and which one is a report. You know where its name has to be unique and which resources have no name-scope at all. You know how to describe a set of objects rather than list one. And you know the exact thing a Secret does and does not do, which is a piece of knowledge a surprising number of working practitioners have wrong.\n=== DIFFICULTY LEGEND CH1 ===\n162:## ⚪ What the KCNA Is, and Who It's For\n186:## ⚪ Ninety Minutes: The Exam as Published\n366:## ⚪ The Phrase We Haven't Defined Yet\n388:## ⚪ How This Book Is Built\n437:Difficulty is marked on section headings: ⚪ Foundation, 🔵 Standard, 🟡 Advanced, 🔴 Expert.\n457:## ⚪ Three Ways to Read This Book","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
